      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did a quick test:\n\n`[]` syntax:\n\n`clang++`: supported\n`g++`: supported\n`clang`: unsupported\n`gcc`: unsupported\n\n`[0]` syntax:\n\n`clang++`: supported\n`g++`: supported\n`clang`: supported\n`gcc`: supported\n\nSo it looks like we should instead do one of two things: either make `FLEXIBLE_ARRAY_MEMBER_SIZE` a C++ thing (instead of being clang specific), or remove `FLEXIBLE_ARRAY_MEMBER_SIZE` entirely, and use `[0]` universally. I would have preference towards the latter, since I don\u0027t see any advantage to `[]` specific to the C++ case here when clang and gcc\u0027s C++ compilers support `[0]` as well.",
      "revId": "b314b67b84022d47b0b41e3089bbe892f2ef58a7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
