      "writtenOn": "2022-09-14T17:37:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the problem is when you use `[0]` as the only struct member you get a zero size struct in C but 1 in C++ so they\u0027re not compatible if you have a .c and a .cc file including the same header. Internal to Google we solve this by always specifying `[1]` and just allocating \"at least one\".",
      "parentUuid": "513e4c80_f38ffcd2",
      "revId": "b314b67b84022d47b0b41e3089bbe892f2ef58a7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
