      "message": "\u003e g++ appears to support  []  so this doesn\u0027t make sense as is\n\nDid you test a a struct that *only* has a flexible array member?\n\nFor example, this fails when compiled with:\n\n```\ng++ -Wall -Werror -std\u003dc++17 -o flexible_array_member flexible_array_member.cc\n```\n\n```\n#include \u003cstdio.h\u003e\n\nint main(int argc, char** argv) {\n  struct Good {\n    int a[];  // Flexible array member\n  };\n  int buffer[10];\n  Good* good \u003d reinterpret_cast\u003cGood*\u003e(buffer);\n  for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c 10; ++i) printf(\"%d\", good-\u003ea[i]);\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\n```\nflexible_array_member.cc: In function ‘int main(int, char**)’:\nflexible_array_member.cc:9:9: error: flexible array member ‘main(int, char**)::Good::a’ in an otherwise empty ‘struct main(int, char**)::Good’\n    9 |     int a[];  // Flexible array member\n      |         ^\n```",
